# The interview clips are Git LFS objects, and Vercel does not support Git LFS.
# A Vercel checkout gets the ~130-byte pointer files, not the video, so shipping
# public/uploads would put corrupt data behind the hero <video> and the interview
# rail — a broken player rather than an honest missing asset.
#
# Excluding them is safe on this host: HomeHero.tsx already renders
# /images/interviews/kalkidan.jpg as the poster, so the hero degrades to a still
# image instead of a dead element.
#
# Production is unaffected. The VPS never gets these bytes from git either —
# tools/deploy.sh ships them once into /srv/remassist/shared/uploads, which lives
# outside every release, and nginx serves them off disk (deploy/README.md).
public/uploads
